(31, 18, 'ICTRIE2026-072.pdf', 'PDF', '952.0 KB', 'uploads/documents/47fdef932b40859eb80f37b4_ICTRIE2026-072.pdf', 'Document', 'Internal Storage', NULL, 0, 0, 3, 'Mr. P . SRISAI\nStudent, Department of AIDS, Saveetha College of Liberal Arts and \nSciences, SIMATS University, Chennai, India\nAn AI-Based Analysis Framework for Digital Eye Strain Detection Using Computer Vision \nand Real-Time Behavioral Analysis (Paper ID: ICTRIE2026-072)\n           Dr. R. Jayakarthik                    Ms. Jayamini Rathnayake      Dr. Gunita Arun Chandhok              Dr. Kularathne   \n           Convenor - SCLAS                             Conveneor - ACHE                   Chairperson - SCLAS            Vice- Chancellor - ACHE\n\nMr. J. THARUN\nStudent, Department of AIDS, Saveetha College of Liberal Arts and \nSciences, SIMATS University, Chennai, India\nAn AI-Based Analysis Framework for Digital Eye Strain Detection Using Computer Vision \nand Real-Time Behavioral Analysis (Paper ID: ICTRIE2026-072)\n           Dr. R. Jayakarthik                    Ms. Jayamini Rathnayake      Dr. Gunita Arun Chandhok              Dr. Kularathne   \n           Convenor - SCLAS                             Conveneor - ACHE                   Chairperson - SCLAS            Vice- Chancellor - ACHE\n\nMr. R. KISHORE\nStudent, Department of AIDS, Saveetha College of Liberal Arts and \nSciences, SIMATS University, Chennai, India\nAn AI-Based Analysis Framework for Digital Eye Strain Detection Using Computer Vision \nand Real-Time Behavioral Analysis (Paper ID: ICTRIE2026-072)\n           Dr. R. Jayakarthik                    Ms. Jayamini Rathnayake      Dr. Gunita Arun Chandhok              Dr. Kularathne   \n           Convenor - SCLAS                             Conveneor - ACHE                   Chairperson - SCLAS            Vice- Chancellor - ACHE', '2026-11-02 08:53:03', '2026-11-02 08:53:03'),
(33, 18, 'Migraine_Care_Guide.pdf', 'PDF', '614.3 KB', 'uploads/documents/4c3ed92bdfa6f46cdcec7e92_Migraine_Care_Guide.pdf', 'Document', 'Internal Storage', 'IMPORTANT', 0, 0, 2, 'MIGRAINE CARE GUIDE \nSimple daily habits to prevent and manage migraine \nShared by Dr. Sindhuja  |  Anesthesiologist, Interventional Pain & Regenerative Specialist \nMigraine is more than \"just a headache\". It often comes with throbbing pain, nausea, and sensitivity to light and \nsound. The good news: small, steady lifestyle habits can reduce how often it strikes. Here is your quick guide. \n1 \nStay Hydrated \n• Sip water regularly through \nthe day \n• Avoid long periods without \nfluids \n• Drink more in hot weather or \nexercise \n• Carry a water bottle with you \n \n2 \nDon\'t Skip Meals \n• Keep regular meal timings \n• Avoid long gaps between \nmeals \n• Keep a healthy snack handy \n• Do not start the day on an \nempty stomach \n \n3 \nMaintain Good Sleep \n• Fixed sleep and wake-up time \n• Avoid frequently changing \nyour schedule \n• Give your body enough rest \n• Switch off screens before bed \n \n4 Know Your Personal Triggers \n \nKeep a simple migraine diary and note down: \n• What you ate \n• Water intake \n• Sleep duration \n• Stress level \n• Screen exposure \n• Time headache started \n• How long it lasted \nDate Food / Water Sleep (hrs) Stress (1-5) Started / Lasted \n          \n          \n \nCommon triggers to watch for: \nDehydration Skipped meals Poor / irregular sleep \nStress & anxiety Long screen time Bright light / loud noise \nStrong smells Too much caffeine Weather change \nHormonal changes (in women)   \n \n5 What To Do During an Attack \n \nRest Lie down in a quiet, dark room if light or sound worsens symptoms \nHydrate Sip water slowly and stay hydrated \nMedicine Follow only the plan prescribed by your doctor \nAvoid triggers Stay away from your known personal triggers\n\nGO TO EMERGENCY IMMEDIATELY IF YOU HAVE \n• Sudden, very severe \"worst ever\" headache \n• Weakness, numbness, or trouble speaking \n• Fever with neck stiffness \n• Sudden vision loss, confusion, or fainting \n• Headache after a head injury \n \nHelpful habits \n• Practise relaxation: deep breathing, yoga, \nmeditation \n• Take screen breaks (every 20-30 minutes) \n• Gentle regular exercise like walking \n• Limit caffeine, and have it at fixed times \n Try to avoid \n• Skipping breakfast or lunch \n• Late-night scrolling and irregular sleep \n• Self-medicating with painkillers again and again \n• Ignoring early warning signs (aura, nausea, light \nsensitivity) \n \n6 When To See a Doctor \n \nSeek medical evaluation if your migraines are: \n• Becoming more frequent \n• Becoming more severe \n• Interfering with your daily activities \n• Needing painkillers more than 2-3 days a week (overuse can worsen headaches) \n \nNeed personal advice? Consult the doctor. \nDr. Sindhuja \nInterventional Pain & Regenerative Specialist \nPhone: 9361366109 \nPalaniappa Hospital, Ramapuram, Chennai \nImportant: Migraine triggers differ from person to person. This guide is for general education and does not replace a medical consultation.', '2026-11-02 09:32:22', '2026-11-02 09:32:22'),
(36, 16, 'Migraine_Care_Guide.pdf', 'PDF', '614.3 KB', 'uploads/documents/10203503014675cbae03f295_Migraine_Care_Guide.pdf', 'Notes', 'Internal Storage', NULL, 0, 0, 2, 'MIGRAINE CARE GUIDE \nSimple daily habits to prevent and manage migraine \nShared by Dr. Sindhuja  |  Anesthesiologist, Interventional Pain & Regenerative Specialist \nMigraine is more than \"just a headache\". It often comes with throbbing pain, nausea, and sensitivity to light and \nsound. The good news: small, steady lifestyle habits can reduce how often it strikes. Here is your quick guide. \n1 \nStay Hydrated \n• Sip water regularly through \nthe day \n• Avoid long periods without \nfluids \n• Drink more in hot weather or \nexercise \n• Carry a water bottle with you \n \n2 \nDon\'t Skip Meals \n• Keep regular meal timings \n• Avoid long gaps between \nmeals \n• Keep a healthy snack handy \n• Do not start the day on an \nempty stomach \n \n3 \nMaintain Good Sleep \n• Fixed sleep and wake-up time \n• Avoid frequently changing \nyour schedule \n• Give your body enough rest \n• Switch off screens before bed \n \n4 Know Your Personal Triggers \n \nKeep a simple migraine diary and note down: \n• What you ate \n• Water intake \n• Sleep duration \n• Stress level \n• Screen exposure \n• Time headache started \n• How long it lasted \nDate Food / Water Sleep (hrs) Stress (1-5) Started / Lasted \n          \n          \n \nCommon triggers to watch for: \nDehydration Skipped meals Poor / irregular sleep \nStress & anxiety Long screen time Bright light / loud noise \nStrong smells Too much caffeine Weather change \nHormonal changes (in women)   \n \n5 What To Do During an Attack \n \nRest Lie down in a quiet, dark room if light or sound worsens symptoms \nHydrate Sip water slowly and stay hydrated \nMedicine Follow only the plan prescribed by your doctor \nAvoid triggers Stay away from your known personal triggers\n\nGO TO EMERGENCY IMMEDIATELY IF YOU HAVE \n• Sudden, very severe \"worst ever\" headache \n• Weakness, numbness, or trouble speaking \n• Fever with neck stiffness \n• Sudden vision loss, confusion, or fainting \n• Headache after a head injury \n \nHelpful habits \n• Practise relaxation: deep breathing, yoga, \nmeditation \n• Take screen breaks (every 20-30 minutes) \n• Gentle regular exercise like walking \n• Limit caffeine, and have it at fixed times \n Try to avoid \n• Skipping breakfast or lunch \n• Late-night scrolling and irregular sleep \n• Self-medicating with painkillers again and again \n• Ignoring early warning signs (aura, nausea, light \nsensitivity) \n \n6 When To See a Doctor \n \nSeek medical evaluation if your migraines are: \n• Becoming more frequent \n• Becoming more severe \n• Interfering with your daily activities \n• Needing painkillers more than 2-3 days a week (overuse can worsen headaches) \n \nNeed personal advice? Consult the doctor. \nDr. Sindhuja \nInterventional Pain & Regenerative Specialist \nPhone: 9361366109 \nPalaniappa Hospital, Ramapuram, Chennai \nImportant: Migraine triggers differ from person to person. This guide is for general education and does not replace a medical consultation.', '2026-11-03 07:03:44', '2026-11-03 07:03:44'),
(37, 18, 'IntelliFile_Project_Document.docx', 'DOCX', '20.3 KB', 'uploads/documents/c6f1b355909dce3c41921048_IntelliFile_Project_Document.docx', 'Notes', 'Internal Storage', NULL, 0, 0, 1, 'INTELLIFILE — AI-BASED INTELLIGENT DOCUMENT PRIORITY SYSTEM\nEXECUTIVE SUMMARY:\nAPP OVERVIEW: IntelliFile is an intelligent document management application that uses AI to automatically read, classify, and prioritize documents so that users always know which file needs attention first. Users can upload or scan documents such as invoices, contracts, notices, certificates, reports, and assignments. The system extracts key details like deadlines, amounts, and keywords, assigns a priority level (High, Medium, or Low), and presents a smart priority dashboard with reminders. Special focus is given to students, working professionals, and small businesses who handle large volumes of documents without dedicated document management staff.\nMARKET RELEVANCE: Individuals and organizations now receive documents through email, messaging apps, cloud drives, and paper, creating information overload. Important files are often buried among unimportant ones, leading to missed deadlines, delayed payments, and wasted search time. Existing storage tools save files but do not understand them. AI-driven document intelligence offers an affordable, scalable, and time-saving solution, making this application highly relevant in the modern digital workplace.\nPROBLEM IT AIMS TO SOLVE:\nInformation overload from too many documents: Users receive large numbers of files daily and cannot quickly identify which ones are urgent or important.\nMissed deadlines and delayed actions: Due dates hidden inside documents are easily overlooked, causing late payments, missed submissions, and lost opportunities.\nManual sorting and organization is time-consuming: Naming, tagging, and arranging files into folders takes significant effort and is often done inconsistently.\nScattered documents across multiple platforms: Files are spread across email, messaging apps, cloud storage, and phone galleries, making it hard to see everything in one place.\nNo intelligent understanding of document content: Traditional storage tools treat all files equally and cannot identify urgency, importance, or required action.\nLack of context-based prioritization and reminders: Priority differs for every user, role, and situation, but existing tools offer only generic or manual flags.\nINTRODUCTION:\nPROBLEM STATEMENT: Modern users handle hundreds of documents, yet most tools only store them without understanding their content or urgency. Priority decisions are made manually, which is slow, inconsistent, and error-prone. As a result, critical documents are delayed or missed while less important files receive attention.\nPURPOSE: The purpose of this application is to provide an AI-powered document priority system that automatically understands document content, ranks documents by importance and urgency, and delivers timely alerts, reducing the time and effort spent on manual sorting and searching.\nSCOPE: The application focuses on document upload and scanning, AI-based text extraction and classification, intelligent priority scoring, deadline tracking, and smart search. It is designed for students, professionals, small businesses, and administrative teams who manage large volumes of documents.\nGPCU\nG – Gap Analysis\nNo automatic prioritization of documents: Existing storage tools list files by name or date and cannot tell which document is most urgent or important.\nDeadlines hidden inside documents: Important dates and amounts remain buried in the text and are not converted into alerts or reminders.\nTime wasted on manual organization: Users spend hours sorting, renaming, and searching for files because there is no automatic classification.\nScattered and duplicate files: Documents spread across platforms and repeated copies create confusion and clutter.\nLack of personalized prioritization: Generic rules do not adapt to the user’s role, habits, and changing priorities.\nP – Product (App)\nSmart document upload and scanning: Users can upload files or scan paper documents with the phone camera, with OCR converting images into searchable text.\nAI-based classification and information extraction: AI identifies the document type (invoice, contract, notice, certificate, etc.) and extracts deadlines, amounts, names, and keywords.\nIntelligent priority scoring: Each document receives a High, Medium, or Low priority score based on urgency, content, document type, and user context, with a short explanation.\nSmart alerts and reminders: The system sends timely notifications for upcoming deadlines and high-priority documents that need action.\nPriority dashboard and smart search: A unified dashboard displays documents ranked by priority, with search by content, type, date, or keyword.\nC – Competition Analysis:\nCompetitor\nType\nLocation\nProduct Offering\nPrice\nBusiness Size\nTarget Audience\nUnique Value Proposition\nManual Filing & Folder Organization\nIndirect\nLocal\nPhysical files, or manually created folders and naming systems on a phone or computer\nLow\nSmall\nIndividuals, students and small offices\nSimple, familiar and no extra cost\nCloud Storage Platforms\nDirect\nGlobal\nOnline storage, folder sync, search and file sharing\nLow to Medium\nLarge\nIndividuals, students and professionals\nAnywhere access and easy sharing\nEnterprise Document Management Systems\nDirect\nGlobal\nWorkflow, version control, approvals and archiving for organizations\nHigh\nLarge\nLarge companies and institutions\nStructured workflows and compliance controls\nEmail Filters & Task Manager Apps\nIndirect\nGlobal\nRule-based labels, flags and to-do lists for documents and attachments\nLow to Medium\nMedium\nWorking professionals and teams\nReminders and manual prioritization\nU – Uniqueness:\nAI-driven automatic prioritization: Ranks documents by understanding their content instead of relying on manual flags or folder names.\nExplainable priority results: Shows the reason for each priority, such as “Payment due in 2 days,” building user trust.\nDeadline extraction and smart reminders: Automatically detects dates and obligations inside documents and converts them into alerts.\nPersonalized learning: Adapts priority decisions over time based on user feedback, role, and behavior.\nOffline scanning and secure processing: Core scanning and viewing features work without continuous internet, with privacy-focused handling of sensitive files.\nFUTURE SCOPE\nMultilingual and regional language support: The system will read and prioritize documents written in multiple languages.\nEmail and messaging integration: Direct import of attachments from email and messaging platforms will bring all documents into one place.\nAutomatic summarization: AI will generate short summaries and key action points for long documents.\nTeam collaboration and workflow: Shared workspaces, task assignment, and approval flows will support teams and organizations.\nDuplicate and version detection: AI will detect similar or repeated documents and manage versions automatically.\nVoice assistant and natural language queries: Users will find documents by asking questions such as “Show my urgent bills this week.”\nWHY USERS WILL USE THIS APP EVEN AFTER TESTING IS DONE\nSaves time every day – Eliminates manual sorting and searching by automatically organizing and ranking documents.\nNever miss an important deadline – Provides timely alerts based on dates and obligations found inside documents.\nPersonalized priority experience – Learns from user feedback and adapts the ranking to individual needs and roles.\nAll documents in one place – Brings files from different sources into a single smart and searchable dashboard.\nReduced stress and improved productivity – Clear priority lists and progress indicators help users focus on what matters most.\nDESIGN AND ENGINEERING STANDARDS\nUser-Centered Design\nSimple and clean interface: The application uses an easy-to-understand layout with color-coded priority labels suitable for users of all technical levels.\nOne-tap upload and scan: Simple actions allow users to add documents quickly without complicated steps.\nAccessibility-friendly design: The system supports readable fonts, clear buttons, high contrast, and inclusive design for elderly and differently-abled users.\nSeparate user and admin dashboards: Dedicated dashboards provide personalized features for individual users and management tools for team administrators.\nSoftware Engineering Practices\nFlutter / Android with MVVM architecture: The app follows structured MVVM design for better maintainability and performance.\nPython backend services: Python (FastAPI) handles authentication, database, AI/NLP processing, and notifications for reliable backend support.\nSecure RESTful API communication: All data exchange is protected using secure HTTPS-based API communication.\nModular and scalable application design: The system is built in modules (OCR, classification, priority engine, notifications), allowing easy upgrades and future feature expansion.\nDATA SECURITY & PRIVACY\nSecure data encryption – User credentials and documents are protected using AES-256 encryption for storage and TLS encryption during data transmission.\nSecure authentication system – Authentication is handled through Firebase Authentication with JWT-based session management to ensure safe and reliable user access.\nPrivacy and data compliance – The system follows GDPR-based data protection principles, including user consent, secure data handling, and activity logging.\nRole-based access control (RBAC) – Only authorized users and team members with granted permissions can view, edit, or share specific documents.\nProtected document storage – Uploaded files and extracted data are stored securely with limited retention, audit trails, and strict privacy controls to safeguard confidentiality.\nPERFORMANCE STANDARDS\nFast AI processing – Optimized OCR, NLP models, and API calls ensure quick document analysis and priority scoring after upload.\nOffline data caching – Caching techniques allow users to access documents, priority lists, and reminders even without continuous internet connectivity.\nTimely push notifications – Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM) delivers deadline reminders and high-priority alerts on time.\nOptimized file handling – Compression and efficient storage maintain document quality while improving speed and reducing data usage.\nEfficient battery management – The application is optimized to minimize battery consumption during camera scanning and background processing.\nTESTING AND QUALITY ASSURANCE\nComprehensive functional testing – Unit testing, integration testing, and UI testing ensure stability across core features such as login, document upload, and priority dashboard.\nAutomated CI/CD testing pipeline – Continuous integration and deployment pipelines automatically test and validate system updates for reliability and performance.\nCross-device compatibility testing – The application is tested across multiple Android and iOS devices to ensure smooth performance on different screen sizes and OS versions.\nScalability and load testing – Load testing validates system performance under increasing users and simultaneous document processing requests.\nAI accuracy testing – Accuracy tests verify OCR quality, document classification, information extraction, and priority scoring against labeled sample documents.\nINTEROPERABILITY STANDARDS\nDocument import/export – Users can import and export documents in PDF, DOCX, JPG/PNG, and CSV report formats for easy sharing and record keeping.\nCloud storage and email integration – The system supports connection with cloud drives and email attachments to collect documents from multiple sources.\nCalendar integration – Extracted deadlines can be synced with calendar applications using standard formats such as iCalendar (.ics).\nETHICAL & TRANSPARENCY STANDARDS\nTransparent AI operation – Users are clearly informed about how AI reads documents, assigns priority, and stores their data, with a visible reason for every priority score.\nUser consent and data permission – In-app consent forms ensure users provide explicit approval before documents are scanned, analyzed, or shared.\nStrict data privacy protection – User documents are never shared with third parties or used to train models without clear permission.\nHuman control over decisions – Users can always review and override AI priority decisions, ensuring the system assists rather than replaces human judgment.\nRELEVANT STANDARDS\nSafety Standards\nISO/IEC 27001 – Information Security Management – Provides guidelines for protecting sensitive information such as personal documents, financial records, and contracts. It ensures secure storage, encryption, and controlled access within the application.\nISO 15489 – Records Management – Defines principles for creating, capturing, classifying, and managing records, supporting reliable organization, retention, and retrieval of documents.\nISO/IEC 23053 – AI System Framework – Supports the design and governance of machine-learning-based systems. It ensures that classification and priority algorithms operate reliably, transparently, and safely.\nISO/IEC 42001 – AI Management System – Provides requirements for responsible management of AI systems, covering risk assessment, accountability, and continuous improvement of the priority engine.\nData Privacy & Security Standards\nGDPR (General Data Protection Regulation) – Ensures that user documents and personal information are collected, stored, and processed with proper user consent and transparency.\nISO/IEC 27701 – Privacy Information Management – Extends ISO 27001 by adding privacy controls for managing sensitive document content and personal information within the system.\nDPDP Act 2023 (India) – Digital Personal Data Protection – Sets rules for lawful processing, consent, and protection of personal data of users in India, guiding how the application handles uploaded documents.\nSoftware & Mobile Application Quality Standards\nISO/IEC 25010 – Software Quality Model – Defines quality attributes such as reliability, usability, performance efficiency, security, and maintainability. This ensures the application provides a stable and effective document platform.\nISO/IEC 29119 – Software Testing Standard – Provides structured guidelines for software testing processes including unit, integration, and system testing to ensure accurate analysis and reliable application performance.\nIEEE 7000 – Ethical Considerations in System Design – Guides the responsible development of AI-driven systems. It ensures fairness, transparency, and ethical behavior when the AI evaluates documents and assigns priority.\nUsability & Accessibility Standards\nISO 9241-210 – Human-Centered Design for Interactive Systems – Ensures the application is designed based on user needs, improving usability and accessibility for people with varied technical skills.\nWCAG 2.1 – Web Content Accessibility Guidelines – Ensures accessible design features such as readable text, clear navigation, and compatibility with assistive technologies.\nISO 9241-11 – Usability Standard – Provides guidelines to ensure the application is easy to use, efficient, and effective for users managing and prioritizing documents.\n2D Design\n[Insert your hand-drawn 2D wireframe here]\nSuggested layout (four panels):\nUSER PROFILE — Name, Age, Phone No, Email, Role (Student / Professional / Business)\nAI ANALYSIS — Document analysis graph, Priority Score (e.g., 84%), Extracted Deadline\nDOCUMENTS — Upload File [Start], Scan Document [Start], Import from Email [Start]\nPRIORITY & ALERTS — High / Medium / Low list, Reminders, Report, Logout\n3D Design\n[Insert your 3D mockup image here]\nSuggested screens: User Profile • AI Document Analysis • Smart Upload & Scan • Priority Dashboard & Alerts\nFUNCTIONAL PROTOTYPE\nIdea Scanning & System Architecture Analysis\nUser onboarding and preference setup – Users register in the application and provide basic details such as role, document types handled, and priority preferences.\nAI-based document analysis and priority generation – The AI backend performs OCR, classifies each document, extracts key information, and automatically generates a priority score and suggested action.\nUser Authentication and Profiles\nSecure authentication system – Provides secure signup, login, and logout with encrypted sessions to ensure safe and reliable user access.\nUser profile management – Allows users to manage personal details such as age, role, notification preferences, and team membership (optional).\nDocument and profile upload – Users can upload profile photos and documents in multiple formats for analysis and organization.\nAI-BASED DOCUMENT PRIORITY MODULE\nDocument capture through mobile interface – Users upload files or scan paper documents with the phone camera for processing.\nAI content analysis – The AI evaluates document type, keywords, dates, amounts, sender, and urgency indicators for precise assessment.\nPriority scoring with explanation – Each document is labeled High, Medium, or Low with a clear reason, such as “Contract expires in 3 days.”\nReal-time suggestions – The system provides instant suggestions such as “Review today,” “Pay before due date,” or “Archive this file.”\nPERSONALIZED PRIORITY LEARNING\nAdaptive AI adjustment – The AI dynamically refines priority rules based on user feedback, corrections, and usage patterns.\nCustomized priority rules – Users can set custom rules, such as marking all documents from a specific sender or category as high priority.\nPROGRESS MONITORING & REPORTS\nVisual dashboard – Daily and weekly charts display pending, completed, and overdue documents by priority level.\nPerformance indicators – Counts of processed documents, deadlines met, and time saved are shown in a simple and understandable format.\nProductivity tracking – Visible progress charts and completion indicators encourage timely action on important documents.\nReport sharing capability – Document summaries and priority reports can be exported and shared with colleagues or supervisors.\nREMINDERS & MOTIVATION SYSTEM\nAutomated deadline reminders – Notifications alert users before due dates and when high-priority documents remain unattended.\nOn-time completion streak tracking – Tracks consecutive days of clearing priority documents to encourage discipline.\nAchievement badges and rewards – Rewards such as “7-Day Zero Overdue Streak” motivate users to stay organized.\nUTILITY & SETTINGS\nUser account controls – Includes Change Password, Edit Profile, Notifications, Logout, and Delete Account for full account management.\nSecure data handling – Ensures strong privacy protection, secure storage, and safe access to user documents and extracted data.\nTESTING AND VALIDATION OF PROTOTYPE\nStructured system workflow validation – The application follows a clear flow: Splash Screen → User Login → Document Upload/Scan → AI Analysis → Priority Dashboard → Admin Dashboard.\nReal-time AI analysis testing – OCR, classification, and priority scoring are validated through a secure API connection with the AI engine.\nUsability and accuracy validation – Testing confirms reliable text extraction, accurate priority results, and an easy-to-use interface suitable for all users.\nSystem reliability verification – Testing verifies system stability, alert delivery, and the effectiveness of personalized priority ranking.\nIMPACT OF PROTOTYPE\nBridging storage and intelligence – The AI-based system moves document handling from simple storage to intelligent understanding, helping users act on the right document at the right time.\nEmpowering productive document management – The system lets users manage documents independently while still allowing optional team sharing and oversight.\nImproving efficiency and accuracy – The prototype reduces time spent on sorting and searching, lowers the risk of missed deadlines, and improves decision-making through intelligent automation.\nCONCLUSION\nIntelliFile — AI-Based Intelligent Document Priority System is more than a basic document storage application — it functions as a smart digital assistant for document management. By providing AI-based content analysis, automatic prioritization, deadline detection, and continuous progress tracking, the system improves productivity, accuracy, and peace of mind. With its scalable AI-driven architecture and user-centered design, the platform has strong potential to expand into email integration, team workflows, and enterprise-grade intelligent document solutions, helping individuals and organizations manage information overload through advanced technology.', '2026-11-03 07:42:03', '2026-11-03 07:42:03');
